vertex. Thus α0 remains an inner vertex throughout. Continue until α=(b1), so its full incident list
exhibits the spur b1b1⁻¹. The source Step1 formally removes it: split into b1d and d⁻¹b1⁻¹X, then
the FULL two-entry vertex permits inverse P1 and gives c and c⁻¹X. To realize the endpoint with
actual proper moves, use the installed ST cancellation for |X|≥2 and the exact five-move
residual-edge subdivision/ST sequence below for |X|1, or replace the formal donor merge by the
